# Desktop Agent — Downloadable Packaging & Distribution

## Background

The agent code in `src/agent/` is already fully built. It:
- Discovers Windows printers via PowerShell / `Win32_Printer` (CIM)
- Polls the server for paid print jobs every 5 seconds
- Downloads the PDF, slices page ranges with `pdf-lib`, and submits to the Windows Print Spooler via `PrintTo` verb
- Serves a local web dashboard at `http://127.0.0.1:4321`
- Persists config at `%LOCALAPPDATA%\PrintivaAgent\config.json`

**The gap:** Shop owners currently need Node.js + npm installed to run it. We need a true **standalone Windows `.exe`** they can just double-click.

---

## Proposed Changes

### 1 — Package the Agent as a Standalone Windows `.exe`

Use [`pkg`](https://github.com/vercel/pkg) to bundle the TypeScript-compiled agent into a self-contained Windows executable (no Node.js required on the shop owner's machine).

> [!IMPORTANT]
> `pkg` requires a compiled JS entry point. We'll add a small build step:
> `tsc --project tsconfig.agent.json` → compiles only `src/agent/` to `dist/agent/`
> then `pkg dist/agent/index.js` → produces `PrintivaAgent.exe`

#### [NEW] `tsconfig.agent.json`
A separate TypeScript config that compiles only `src/agent/` to `dist/agent/`, targeting CommonJS (required by pkg).

#### [NEW] `agent.pkg.json`
`pkg` configuration specifying:
- Entry: `dist/agent/index.js`
- Target: `node20-win-x64`
- Output: `dist/PrintivaAgent.exe`
- Assets: include `pdf-lib` wasm assets if any

#### [MODIFY] [`package.json`](file:///c:\Users\user\Downloads\Printiva\package.json)
Add new scripts:
```json
"build:agent":   "tsc --project tsconfig.agent.json && pkg dist/agent/index.js --config agent.pkg.json --output dist/PrintivaAgent.exe --target node20-win-x64",
"agent":         "tsx src/agent/index.ts"   ← already fixed
```

