## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Where will the `.exe` be hosted for download?**
>
> - **Option A (Recommended):** GitHub Releases — build the exe via a GitHub Actions workflow on each tag push. The download API route redirects to the latest release URL.
> - **Option B:** Serve directly from the Next.js server (`/api/agent/download`). Simple but adds ~50 MB to the server. Fine for small-scale deployment.
> - **Option C:** A cloud storage bucket (Supabase Storage or S3).

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Should the agent run as a background Windows Service or as a tray app?**
>
> - **Option A (Current):** Console window + browser dashboard at port 4321. Shop owner opens it manually.
> - **Option B:** System tray icon (requires Electron or a separate tray library). Heavier but more user-friendly.
> - **Option C:** Windows Service via NSSM (Non-Sucking Service Manager) — runs silently in background, survives reboots.

